#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:204
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Rust"
msgstr "Instalação do Rust"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:207
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To install into the <filename class=\"directory\">/opt</filename> directory,"
" remove any existing <filename>/opt/rustc</filename> symlink and create a "
"new directory (i.e. with a different name if trying a modified build of the "
"same version).  As the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"Para instalar no diretório &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt</filename>&quot;, remova qualquer link simbólico "
"&quot;<filename>/opt/rustc</filename>&quot; existente e crie um novo "
"diretório (ou seja, com um nome diferente se tentar uma construção "
"modificada da mesma versão). Como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:216
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir -pv /opt/rustc-&rust-version;      &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -svfn rustc-&rust-version; /opt/rustc</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir -pv /opt/rustc-&rust-version;     &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -svfn rustc-&rust-version; /opt/rustc</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:221
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If multiple versions of <application>Rust</application> are installed in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt</filename>, changing to another version "
"only requires changing the <filename> /opt/rustc</filename> symbolic link "
"and then running <command>ldconfig</command>."
msgstr ""
"Se múltiplas versões do &quot;<application>Rust</application>&quot; "
"estiverem instaladas em &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt</filename>&quot;, [então] a mudança para outra "
"versão exige somente mudar o link simbólico "
"&quot;<filename>/opt/rustc</filename>&quot; e então executar "
"&quot;<command>ldconfig</command>&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:229
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create a suitable <filename>config.toml</filename> file which will configure"
" the build."
msgstr ""
"Crie um arquivo &quot;<filename>config.toml</filename>&quot; adequado que "
"configurará a construção."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:233
#, no-wrap, xml-text
#| msgid ""
#| "<userinput>cat &lt;&lt; EOF &gt; config.toml\n"
#| "<literal># see config.toml.example for more possible options\n"
#| "# See the 8.4 book for an old example using shipped LLVM\n"
#| "# e.g. if not installing clang, or using a version before 13.0\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Tell x.py the editors have reviewed the content of this file\n"
#| "# and updated it to follow the major changes of the building system,\n"
#| "# so x.py will not warn us to do such a review.\n"
#| "change-id = 133207\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[llvm]\n"
#| "# When using system llvm prefer shared libraries\n"
#| "link-shared = true\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Do not download pre-built LLVM, instead either use the system\n"
#| "# LLVM or build LLVM from the shipped source.\n"
#| "download-ci-llvm = false\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# If building the shipped LLVM source, only enable the x86 target\n"
#| "# instead of all the targets supported by LLVM.\n"
#| "targets = \"X86\"\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[build]\n"
#| "# omit docs to save time and space (default is to build them)\n"
#| "docs = false\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# install extended tools: cargo, clippy, etc\n"
#| "extended = true\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Do not query new versions of dependencies online.\n"
#| "locked-deps = true\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Specify which extended tools (those from the default install).\n"
#| "tools = [\"cargo\", \"clippy\", \"rustdoc\", \"rustfmt\"]\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Use the source code shipped in the tarball for the dependencies.\n"
#| "# The combination of this and the \"locked-deps\" entry avoids downloading\n"
#| "# many crates from Internet, and makes the Rustc build more stable.\n"
#| "vendor = true\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[install]\n"
#| "prefix = \"/opt/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
#| "docdir = \"share/doc/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[rust]\n"
#| "channel = \"stable\"\n"
#| "description = \"for BLFS &version;\"\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Enable the same optimizations as the official upstream build.\n"
#| "lto = \"thin\"\n"
#| "codegen-units = 1\n"
#| "\n"
#| "# Don't download compiler components from the upstream CI:\n"
#| "# it's only intended for developers working on standard library\n"
#| "# and tools, and it only works with the Rust Git repository.\n"
#| "download-rustc = false\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
#| "llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"\n"
#| "\n"
#| "[target.i686-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
#| "llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"</literal>\n"
#| "EOF</userinput>"
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &lt;&lt; EOF &gt; config.toml\n"
"<literal># see config.toml.example for more possible options\n"
"# See the 8.4 book for an old example using shipped LLVM\n"
"# e.g. if not installing clang, or using a version before 13.0\n"
"\n"
"# Tell x.py the editors have reviewed the content of this file\n"
"# and updated it to follow the major changes of the building system,\n"
"# so x.py will not warn us to do such a review.\n"
"change-id = 134650\n"
"\n"
"[llvm]\n"
"# When using system llvm prefer shared libraries\n"
"link-shared = true\n"
"\n"
"# Do not download pre-built LLVM, instead either use the system\n"
"# LLVM or build LLVM from the shipped source.\n"
"download-ci-llvm = false\n"
"\n"
"# If building the shipped LLVM source, only enable the x86 target\n"
"# instead of all the targets supported by LLVM.\n"
"targets = \"X86\"\n"
"\n"
"[build]\n"
"# omit docs to save time and space (default is to build them)\n"
"docs = false\n"
"\n"
"# install extended tools: cargo, clippy, etc\n"
"extended = true\n"
"\n"
"# Do not query new versions of dependencies online.\n"
"locked-deps = true\n"
"\n"
"# Specify which extended tools (those from the default install).\n"
"tools = [\"cargo\", \"clippy\", \"rustdoc\", \"rustfmt\"]\n"
"\n"
"[install]\n"
"prefix = \"/opt/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
"docdir = \"share/doc/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
"\n"
"[rust]\n"
"channel = \"stable\"\n"
"description = \"for BLFS &version;\"\n"
"\n"
"# Enable the same optimizations as the official upstream build.\n"
"lto = \"thin\"\n"
"codegen-units = 1\n"
"\n"
"[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"\n"
"\n"
"[target.i686-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &lt;&lt; EOF &gt; config.toml\n"
"<literal># see config.toml.example for more possible options\n"
"# See the 8.4 book for an old example using shipped LLVM\n"
"# e.g. if not installing clang, or using a version before 13.0\n"
"\n"
"# Tell x.py the editors have reviewed the content of this file\n"
"# and updated it to follow the major changes of the building system,\n"
"# so x.py will not warn us to do such a review.\n"
"change-id = 134650\n"
"\n"
"[llvm]\n"
"# When using system llvm prefer shared libraries\n"
"link-shared = true\n"
"\n"
"# Do not download pre-built LLVM, instead either use the system\n"
"# LLVM or build LLVM from the shipped source.\n"
"download-ci-llvm = false\n"
"\n"
"# If building the shipped LLVM source, only enable the x86 target\n"
"# instead of all the targets supported by LLVM.\n"
"targets = \"X86\"\n"
"\n"
"[build]\n"
"# omit docs to save time and space (default is to build them)\n"
"docs = false\n"
"\n"
"# install extended tools: cargo, clippy, etc\n"
"extended = true\n"
"\n"
"# Do not query new versions of dependencies online.\n"
"locked-deps = true\n"
"\n"
"# Specify which extended tools (those from the default install).\n"
"tools = [\"cargo\", \"clippy\", \"rustdoc\", \"rustfmt\"]\n"
"\n"
"[install]\n"
"prefix = \"/opt/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
"docdir = \"share/doc/rustc-&rust-version;\"\n"
"\n"
"[rust]\n"
"channel = \"stable\"\n"
"description = \"for BLFS &version;\"\n"
"\n"
"# Enable the same optimizations as the official upstream build.\n"
"lto = \"thin\"\n"
"codegen-units = 1\n"
"\n"
"[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"\n"
"\n"
"[target.i686-unknown-linux-gnu]\n"
"llvm-config = \"/usr/bin/llvm-config\"</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:303
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now remove some tests triggering a full rebuild of the Rust standard library"
" and compiler:"
msgstr ""
"Agora remova alguns testes que deflagram uma reconstrução completa da "
"biblioteca padrão e do compilador Rust:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:307
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed '/MirOpt/d' -i "
"src/bootstrap/src/core/builder/mod.rs</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed '/MirOpt/d' -i "
"src/bootstrap/src/core/builder/mod.rs</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:310
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Compile <application>Rust</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Compile &quot;<application>Rust</application>&quot; executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#.  fixed in 1.58.0, retain as a reminder that fixed crates can be used
#. <screen>
#. <userinput>sed -i -e '/^curl /s/0.4.38/0.4.40/' #.        -e '/^curl-sys
#. /s/0.4.48/0.4.50/' #.        src/tools/cargo/Cargo.toml &amp;&amp;
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:319
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>[ ! -e /usr/include/libssh2.h ] || export LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1\n"
"[ ! -e /usr/include/sqlite3.h ] || export LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1\n"
"./x.py build</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>[ ! -e /usr/include/libssh2.h ] || export LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1\n"
"[ ! -e /usr/include/sqlite3.h ] || export LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1\n"
"./x.py build</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:325
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The test suite will generate some messages in the <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">system log</phrase> <phrase revision=\"systemd\">systemd "
"journal</phrase> for traps on invalid opcodes, and for segmentation faults."
"  In themselves these are nothing to worry about, just a way for the test to"
" be terminated."
msgstr ""
"A suíte de teste gerará algumas mensagens no <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\">registro do sistema</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\">diário do systemd</phrase> para interceptações em "
"códigos inválidos de operação e para falhas de segmentação. Por si só, isso "
"não é motivo de preocupação, apenas uma maneira do teste ser terminado."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:335
#, xml-text
msgid "To run the tests (again using all available CPUs) issue:"
msgstr ""
"Para executar os testes (novamente usando todas as &quot;CPUs&quot; "
"disponíveis), emita:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:338
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./x.py test --verbose --no-fail-fast | tee rustc-"
"testlog</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>./x.py test --verbose --no-fail-fast | tee rustc-"
"testlog</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:341
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Six tests in the bootstrap test suite are known to fail because they expect "
"to run in the Rust Git repository."
msgstr ""
"Seis testes na suíte de teste de instruções de autoaprimoramento são "
"conhecidos por falharem porque eles esperam executar no repositório Git da "
"Rust."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:354
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As with all large test suites, some tests might fail on some machines - if "
"the number of additional failures is low, check the log for 'failures:' and "
"review lines above that, particularly the 'stderr:' lines. Any mention of "
"SIGSEGV or signal 11 in a failing test is a cause for concern."
msgstr ""
"Tal como acontece com todas as grandes suítes de teste, alguns testes podem "
"falhar em algumas máquinas - se o número de falhas adicionais for baixo, "
"verifique se existem 'failures:' no registro e revise as linhas acima, "
"especialmente as linhas 'stderr:'. Qualquer menção ao SIGSEGV ou ao sinal "
"onze (11) em um teste falho é motivo de preocupação."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:362
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you get any <emphasis>other</emphasis> failing test which reports an "
"issue number then you should search for that issue.  For example, when rustc"
" &gt;= 1.41.1 was built with a version of sysllvm before 10.0 the test for "
"issue 69225 failed <ulink url=\"https://github.com/rust-"
"lang/rust/issues/69225\"/> and that should be regarded as a critical failure"
" (they released 1.41.1 because of it).  Most other failures will not be "
"critical."
msgstr ""
"Se você receber algum <emphasis>outro</emphasis> teste falho que informe um "
"número de problema, então você deveria procurar por esse problema. Por "
"exemplo, quando &quot;Rustc&quot; &gt;= 1.41.1 era construído com uma versão"
" do &quot;LLVM&quot; do sistema anterior à 10.0, o teste para o problema "
"&quot;69225&quot; falhava <ulink url=\"https://github.com/rust-"
"lang/rust/issues/69225\"/> e isso deveria ser considerado como uma falha "
"crítica (eles(as) lançaram 1.41.1 por causa disso). A maioria das outras "
"falhas não será crítica."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:372
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Therefore, you should determine the number of failures.  The number of tests"
" which passed and failed can be found by running:"
msgstr ""
"Portanto, você deveria determinar o número de falhas. O número de testes que"
" passaram e falharam pode ser encontrado executando-se:"

#.  split into two lines for narrower screen windows
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:377
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>grep '^test result:' rustc-testlog |\n"
" awk '{sum1 += $4; sum2 += $6} END { print sum1 \" passed; \" sum2 \" failed\" }'</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>grep '^test result:' rustc-testlog |\n"
" awk '{sum1 += $4; sum2 += $6} END { print sum1 \" passed; \" sum2 \" failed\" }'</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:381
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The other available fields are $8 for those which were ignored (i.e. "
"skipped), $10 for 'measured' and $12 for 'filtered out' but both those last "
"two are probably zero."
msgstr ""
"Os outros campos disponíveis são &quot;$8&quot; para aqueles que foram "
"ignorados (ou seja, pulados), &quot;$10&quot; para 'medido' e "
"&quot;$12&quot; para 'filtrado', mas ambos os dois últimos provavelmente "
"sejam zero."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:387
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the &root; user, install the package:"
msgstr "Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;&root;&quot;, instale o pacote:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:392
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If <command>sudo</command> or <command>su</command> is invoked for switching"
" to the &root; user, ensure <envar>LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</envar> and "
"<envar>LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</envar> are correctly passed or the "
"following command may rebuild <command>cargo</command> with shipped copies "
"of libssh2 and sqlite.  For <command>sudo</command>, use the "
"<option>--preserve-env=LIB{SSH2,SQLITE3}_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</option> option."
"  For <command>su</command>, do <emphasis>not</emphasis> use the "
"<option>-</option> or <option>--login</option> options."
msgstr ""
"Se <command>sudo</command> ou <command>su</command> for invocado para "
"comutar para o(a) usuário(a) &root;, certifique-se de que "
"<envar>LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</envar> e "
"<envar>LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</envar> sejam passados corretamente ou "
"o comando a seguir pode reconstruir <command>cargo</command> com cópias "
"enviadas de libssh2 e sqlite. Para <command>sudo</command>, use a opção "
"<option>--preserve-env=LIB{SSH2,SQLITE3}_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</option>. Para "
"<command>su</command>, <emphasis>não</emphasis> use as opções "
"<option>-</option> ou <option>--login</option>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:405
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>./x.py install rustc std &amp;&amp;\n"
"./x.py install --stage=1 cargo clippy rustfmt</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>./x.py install rustc std &amp;&amp;\n"
"./x.py install --stage=1 cargo clippy rustfmt</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:409
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Still as the &root; user, fix the installation of documentation, symlink a "
"<application>Zsh</application> completion file into the correct location, "
"and move a <application>Bash</application> completion file into the location"
" recommended by the <application>Bash</application> completion maintainers:"
msgstr ""
"Ainda como o(a) usuário(a) &root;, corrija a instalação da documentação, "
"linque simbolicamente um arquivo de completação do "
"<application>Zsh</application> para o local correto, e mova um arquivo de "
"completação do <application>Bash</application> para o local recomendado "
"pelos(as) mantenedores(as) da completação do "
"<application>Bash</application>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:417
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>rm -fv /opt/rustc-&rust-version;/share/doc/rustc-&rust-version;/*.old   &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -vm644 README.md                                \\\n"
"               /opt/rustc-&rust-version;/share/doc/rustc-&rust-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"install -vdm755 /usr/share/zsh/site-functions      &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /opt/rustc/share/zsh/site-functions/_cargo \\\n"
"        /usr/share/zsh/site-functions\n"
"\n"
"mv -v /etc/bash_completion.d/cargo /usr/share/bash-completion/completions</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>rm -fv /opt/rustc-&rust-version;/share/doc/rustc-&rust-version;/*.old   &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -vm644 README.md                                \\\n"
"               /opt/rustc-&rust-version;/share/doc/rustc-&rust-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"install -vdm755 /usr/share/zsh/site-functions      &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /opt/rustc/share/zsh/site-functions/_cargo \\\n"
"        /usr/share/zsh/site-functions\n"
"\n"
"mv -v /etc/bash_completion.d/cargo /usr/share/bash-completion/completions</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:428
#, xml-text
msgid "Finally, unset the exported environment variables:"
msgstr "Finalmente, desconfigure as variáveis de ambiente exportadas:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:431
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>unset LIB{SSH2,SQLITE3}_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>unset LIB{SSH2,SQLITE3}_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:436
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:439
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>ln -svfn rustc-&rust-version; /opt/rustc</command>: if this is not "
"the first use of the <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/rustc</filename> "
"symlink, overwrite it by forcing, and use the '-n' flag to avoid getting "
"confusing results from e.g. <command>ls -l</command>."
msgstr ""
"<command>ln -svfn rustc-&rust-version; /opt/rustc</command>: se esse não for"
" o primeiro uso do link simbólico <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/rustc</filename>, [então] sobrescreva-o forçando e "
"use o sinalizador '-n' para evitar resultados confusos oriundos, por "
"exemplo, de <command>ls -l</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:446
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>targets = \"X86\"</literal>: this avoids building all the available"
" linux cross-compilers (AArch64, MIPS, PowerPC, SystemZ, etc). "
"Unfortunately, rust insists on installing source files for these below "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/rustc/lib/src</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<literal>targets = \"X86\"</literal>: isso evita construir todos os "
"compiladores cruzados disponíveis do Linux (AArch64, MIPS, PowerPC, SystemZ,"
" etc). Infelizmente, o Rust insiste em instalar os arquivos fonte para esses"
" abaixo de <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/rustc/lib/src</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:453
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>extended = true</literal>: this installs several tools (specified "
"by the <literal>tools</literal> entry) alongside <command>rustc</command>."
msgstr ""
"<literal>extended = true</literal>: isso instala várias ferramentas "
"(especificadas pela entrada <literal>tools</literal>) juntamente com o "
"<command>rustc</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:459
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>tools = [\"cargo\", \"clippy\", \"rustdoc\", "
"\"rustfmt\"]</literal>: only build the tools from the 'default' profile in "
"binary command <command>rustup</command> which are recommended for most "
"users.  The other tools are unlikely to be useful unless using (old) code "
"analyzers or editing the standard library."
msgstr ""
"<literal>tools = [\"cargo\", \"clippy\", \"rustdoc\", "
"\"rustfmt\"]</literal>: construa somente as ferramentas a partir do perfil "
"'padrão' no comando binário <command>rustup</command> que é recomendado para"
" a maioria dos(as) usuários(as). As outras ferramentas são improváveis que "
"sejam úteis, a menos que se use analisadores (antigos) de código ou se edite"
" a biblioteca padrão."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:467
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>channel = \"stable\"</literal>: this ensures only stable features "
"can be used, the default in <filename>config.toml</filename> is to use "
"development features, which is not appropriate for a released version."
msgstr ""
"<literal>channel = \"stable\"</literal>: isso garante que somente recursos "
"estáveis possam ser usados. O padrão no <filename>config.toml</filename> é o"
" de usar recursos de desenvolvimento, o que não é apropriado para uma versão"
" lançada."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:474
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]</literal>: the syntax of "
"<filename>config.toml</filename> requires an <literal>llvm-config</literal> "
"entry for each target for which system-llvm is to be used. Change the target"
" to <literal>[target.i686-unknown-linux-gnu]</literal> if you are building "
"on 32-bit x86. This whole section may be omitted if you wish to build "
"against the shipped llvm, or do not have clang, but the resulting build will"
" be larger and take longer."
msgstr ""
"<literal>[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]</literal>: a sintaxe do "
"<filename>config.toml</filename> exige uma entrada <literal>llvm-"
"config</literal> para cada alvo para o qual o LLVM do sistema esteja para "
"ser usado. Mude o alvo para <literal>[target.i686-unknown-linux-"
"gnu]</literal> se você estiver construindo em x86 de 32 bits. Essa seção "
"inteira pode ser omitida se você desejar construir contra o LLVM enviado ou "
"não tiver clang, mas a construção resultante será maior e demorará mais."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:493
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>export LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1</command>: Allow "
"<command>cargo</command> to link to system libssh2."
msgstr ""
"<command>export LIBSSH2_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1</command>: Permite que o "
"&quot;<command>cargo</command>&quot; se vincule à &quot;libssh2&quot; do "
"sistema."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:502
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>export LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1</command>: Allow "
"<command>cargo</command> to link to system sqlite."
msgstr ""
"<command>export LIBSQLITE3_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1</command>: Permite "
"<command>cargo</command> lincar ao sqlite do sistema."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:516
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--verbose</parameter>: this switch can sometimes provide more "
"information about a test which fails."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--verbose</parameter>: essa chave às vezes pode fornecer mais "
"informações relativas a um teste que falhe."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:521
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--no-fail-fast</parameter>: this switch ensures that the test "
"suite will not stop at the first error."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--no-fail-fast</parameter>: essa chave garante que a suíte de "
"teste não parará no primeiro erro."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:527
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--stage=1</parameter>: this switch works around an issue causing "
"some Rustc components unnecessarily rebuilt running <command>./x.py "
"install</command>."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--stage=1</parameter>: essa chave contorna um problema que faz "
"com que alguns componentes do Rustc sejam reconstruídos desnecessariamente "
"ao se executar <command>./x.py install</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:535
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Rust"
msgstr "Configurando o Rust"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:538
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr "Informação de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:541
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you installed <application>rustc</application> in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt</filename>, you need to update the following "
"configuration files so that <application>rustc</application> is correctly "
"found by other packages and system processes."
msgstr ""
"Se você instalou &quot;<application>rustc</application>&quot; em "
"&quot;<filename class=\"directory\">/opt</filename>&quot;, [então] você "
"precisa atualizar os seguintes arquivos de configuração, de forma que "
"&quot;<application>rustc</application>&quot; seja encontrado corretamente "
"por outros pacotes e processos do sistema."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:548
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user, create the "
"<filename>/etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</filename> file:"
msgstr ""
"Como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;, crie o arquivo "
"&quot;<filename>/etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</filename>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:552
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh\n"
"\n"
"pathprepend /opt/rustc/bin           PATH\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh\n"
"\n"
"pathprepend /opt/rustc/bin           PATH\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:561
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Immediately after installation, update the current PATH for your current "
"shell as a normal user:"
msgstr ""
"Imediatamente depois da instalação, atualize o PATH atual para teu shell "
"atual como um(a) usuário(a) normal:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:565
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>source /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>source /etc/profile.d/rustc.sh</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:572
#, xml-text
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "Conteúdo"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><segmentedlist><segtitle>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:575
#, xml-text
msgid "Installed Programs"
msgstr "Aplicativos Instalados"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><segmentedlist><segtitle>
#: blfs-en/general/prog/rust.xml:576
